What is a feedback loop and why is it essential?
Answer:
A feedback loop is a structured mechanism that converts outcomes into system improvements. It consists of three parts: signal collection, interpretation, and deliberate adjustment.
Without feedback loops, systems stagnate. Experts engineer learning so improvement continues even when individuals change.

